  "id": "Compound::DB06228 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Rivaroxaban is linked to Abcb1 through a series of molecular and physiological interactions. The evidence suggests that Rivaroxaban causes conditions such as haemarthrosis, wound hemorrhage, and compartment syndrome, all of which are associated with Ticagrelor. Ticagrelor, in turn, binds to Abcb1, indicating a potential mechanism by which Rivaroxaban indirectly influences Abcb1 activity. This relationship is supported by the shared lowest common ancestors of Rivaroxaban and Ticagrelor, both of which are classified under the category of organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and agents affecting blood or body fluid. The consistent pathway through Ticagrelor highlights a critical role in the interaction between Rivaroxaban and Abcb1, suggesting a possible regulatory or modulatory effect on Abcb1 function. The integration of these findings underscores a mechanistic link that is both biologically plausible and contextually relevant.",
